deep.reconstruction:
Setting: Grothendieck's 1986 axiomatics of an 'atelier' M. M is a structure of 'figures' (lieux) X, Y, F, G, ... with these relations:
- a part relation G ≤ F (or G ⊂ F);
- a refinement relation X' ≪ X;
- for Y ≤ X and X' ≪ X, an induced refinement X'_Y = X'|Y with X'_Y ≤ X' and X'_Y ≪ Y;
- a compatibility relation between figures, written with the 'between' symbol (≷);
- intersections ∩ and unions/gluings ∪.
The poset of refinements of X is written X̃.

What p.75 does: it attacks the non-trivial direction of a gluing proposition. Take F' ≪ F and G' ≪ G whose restrictions to K = F ∩ G are compatible, with H'_K = F'_K ∨ G'_K ≪ K (by Ax 4). The aim is to build a refinement of F ∪ G. The plan:
- glue F' with H'_K to get H'_F, and G' with H'_K to get H'_G;
- check that both restrict to H'_K on K;
- apply the gluing axiom (recollement) to get H' = H'_F ∪ H'_G.
This reduces everything to the special case G ⊂ F.

This page, first statement ('Cor. Main', possibly a misreading of 'Conj.'). Let G ≤ F and F' ≪ F, inducing F'_G on G. Let G' ≪ G with F'_G ≤ G'. Then F' and G' are compatible, and F' ∩ G' = F'_G. Grothendieck immediately asks whether this follows from the other axioms. He then restates it in standard form, in what was At 11 and is renamed At 11': for X ⊃ Y, X' ≪ X, Y' ≪ Y, if X'_Y is compatible with Y', then X' is compatible with Y'. In words, compatibility of a refinement of the big figure with a refinement of a sub-figure can be tested after restriction to the sub-figure.

His assessment: this is a considerable strengthening of At 10 (the disjunction criterion by the lieux). It would also follow from At 9' + At 10, or from At 9'' + At 10 (the compatibility criteria).

He then proposes a more general axiom, At 12, which implies At 11' and, mutatis mutandis, At 11. Let X' ≪ X and Y' ≪ Y with X ≷ Y, and K = X ∩ Y. This gives induced refinements X'_K ≤ X' with X'_K ≪ K, and Y'_K ≤ Y' with Y'_K ≪ K. If X'_K and Y'_K are compatible, then X' and Y' are compatible. The next page gives a contrapositive form quantifying over all X'' in the refinement poset of X' and all Y'' in that of Y'. On that page At 12 is said to imply At 11', At 10, the proposition of p.73, and Cor. 2 p.69. It is then folded into the notion of a Σ-atelier: each refinement poset X̃ must lie in a prescribed full subcategory Σ of ordered sets.

What it serves: a 'locality of compatibility' axiom, i.e. compatibility of refinements is decided on overlaps. It plays the role of the amalgamation/gluing condition needed to make refinements glue like a sheaf over unions of figures. Typical model: PL-type subdivisions of polyhedra in a tame-topology framework.
